ent-ClothingUniformBluedress = light blue dress
    .desc = A simple light blue dress, tailored to flatter the figure.

ent-ClothingUniformCourtesandress = courtesan dress
    .desc = A luxurious dress designed to attract attention, often worn by courtesans.

ent-ClothingUniformGreendress = light green dress
    .desc = A simple light green dress, tailored to flatter the figure.

ent-ClothingUniformMaiddressfancy = valorian maid dress
    .desc = A dress befitting the housekeeper of a lord's staff. While not as intricate as a royal's, it is indicative of the house's status.

ent-ClothingUniformMaidgown = maid gown
    .desc = A dress worn by those of manors and noble staff. Commonly black, though some estates dye them to their house colors.

ent-ClothingUniformNightgown = nightgown
    .desc = An elegant and enticing nightgown, made for comfort and allure.

ent-ClothingUniformNobledress = noble's pinafore
    .desc = A comfortable dress adapted from simpler garments often worn by working-class women.

ent-ClothingUniformSilkydress = silky dress
    .desc = Despite not actually being made of silk, the legendary expertise needed to sew this puts the quality on par.

ent-ClothingUniformTaverndress = tavern dress
    .desc = A simple green dress with a corset, its skirt has slits for easy movement.

ent-ClothingUniformVelvetdress = velvet dress
    .desc = A garment made with embroidered velvet, both elegant and warm. Poetry made manifest in swaying fabric.
